<PageLayout title="Smart Search Engine — TotalRecalls" description="Smart Search Engine is an add-on for TotalRecalls Pro. It indexes your Library on your PC so you can search eight providers' conversations in plain English — nothing is uploaded." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Previews", href: "/previews/" }, { label: "Smart Search Engine" }]}>
  <h1>Smart Search Engine</h1>
  <p>Smart Search Engine is now available as an add-on for TotalRecalls Pro. It indexes your Library on your PC so you can search eight providers' conversations in plain English — no upload, no cloud service. See <a href="/smart-search/">Smart Search Engine</a>.</p>
  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A local index built from your exported Markdown, stored beside your archive.</li>
    <li>Questions answered with citations back to the exact conversation and the lines that matched.</li>
    <li>Keyword search that works immediately, with semantic ranking layered on once the index is built.</li>
    <li>Re-indexing increments as new exports land, rather than rebuilding from scratch.</li>
    <li>Everything runs on your machine; no query and no document ever leaves it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Want to try it? <a href="/buy/">Buy the bundle</a> or <a href="/smart-search/">learn more about Smart Search Engine</a>.</p>
</PageLayout>
